==English==

===Etymology===
* From the boundary line on a graph of an aircraft's capabilities, especially those of height and speed.
* {{term|push}} + {{term|the}} + {{term|envelope}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[push]] the [[envelope]]}}

# {{context|intransitive|idiomatic|lang=en}} to go [[beyond]] [[established]] [[limit]]s; to [[pioneer]].
#: ''They '''pushed the envelope''' on pricing derivatives.''

